  "explanation": "The fsync() function in C is used to force all buffered modifications to a file descriptor to be written to the physical storage device. It ensures that data is durably stored on disk, which is essential for applications requiring data integrity and reliability, such as file systems or databases, to prevent data loss in case of crashes or power failures.",
